cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the released artefacts, please cite the technical report."
title: "Reranker-Free Edge Retrieval: Distilling Contextual Chunk Enrichment into a 0.6B Model"
abstract: >-
  Contextual retrieval enriches each chunk with a short document-level summary
  before indexing and is usually paired with a cross-encoder reranker. This work
  shows that on a small, homogeneous, non-English corpus a dense-only index of
  distilled on-device contexts comes within 0.05 recall@10 of the same index
  with a 0.6B cross-encoder, an interval that includes zero, at 1/1322 of the
  query latency, and that the API teacher can be distilled into a 0.6B model
  that regenerates the corpus on the device.
type: software
